stream
0.8 w 30.00 38.00 535.28 765.89 re S
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 280.14 22.00 Tm (Page 12) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 772.00 Tm (6. RELATIONAL DATABASE DESIGN) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 735.00 Tm (The relational design separates authentication, student profiles, companies, job) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 717.00 Tm (openings, applications, and interviews into independent but connected tables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 699.00 Tm (This design reduces duplication and supports reliable joins for reports and) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 681.00 Tm (dashboards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 655.00 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 655.00 Tm (Primary keys identify each record uniquely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 632.00 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 632.00 Tm (Foreign keys preserve relationships between dependent records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 609.00 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 609.00 Tm (Unique constraints prevent duplicate accounts, roll numbers, company names,) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 591.00 Tm (and repeated applications.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 568.00 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 568.00 Tm (Status fields support controlled workflow tracking for jobs, applications, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 74.00 550.00 Tm (interviews.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
