31 0 obj
<< /Length 1114 >>
stream
0.8 w 30.00 38.00 535.28 765.89 re S
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 280.14 22.00 Tm (Page 13) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 772.00 Tm (7. DATABASE NORMALIZATION) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 735.00 Tm (First Normal Form \(1NF\): All fields contain atomic values, and every table has a) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 717.00 Tm (primary key. For example, student roll number, department, CGPA, and phone number) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 699.00 Tm (are stored as separate attributes instead of combined text.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 673.00 Tm (Second Normal Form \(2NF\): Non-key attributes depend on the full key of their) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 655.00 Tm (table. Job details depend on job id, company details depend on company id, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 637.00 Tm (application status depends on the application record.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 611.00 Tm (The applications table also resolves the many-to-many relationship between) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 593.00 Tm (students and jobs, preventing repeated groups inside the students or jobs tables.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
